    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-consequential-amendments-act-2000-sch-1-sec-10a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "10A Consultation with Gene Technology Regulator",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-consequential-amendments-act-2000#sch-1-sec-10a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "gene-technology-consequential-amendments-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "gene-technology-consequential-amendments-act-2000.pdf, p.11",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies to the following:\n\n(a) an assessment of an industrial chemical that is, or contains, a\nGM product;\n\n(b) an application for a permit (however described) in relation to\nan industrial chemical that is, or contains, a GM product.\n\n(2) Subject to subsection (5), the Director must give written notice to\nthe Gene Technology Regulator:\n\n(a) stating that the assessment is to be undertaken, or that the\napplication for the permit has been made, as the case\nrequires; and\n\n(b) requesting the Gene Technology Regulator to give advice\nabout the assessment or the application for the permit.\n\n(3) If the Director gives the Gene Technology Regulator a notice under\nsubsection (2), the Gene Technology Regulator may give written\nadvice to the Director about the assessment or the application.\n\n(4) The advice is to be given within the period specified in the notice.\n\n(5) If an advice from the Gene Technology Regulator is in force under\nsection 10B in relation to a class of GM products, the Director is\nnot required to notify the Regulator under this section in relation\nto:\n\n(a) an assessment of an industrial chemical that is or contains a\nGM product belonging to that class; or\n\n(b) an application for a permit in respect of an industrial\nchemical that is or contains a GM product belonging to that\nclass.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies to the following:\n\n(a) an assessment of an industrial chemical that is, or contains, a\nGM product;\n\n(b) an application for a permit (however described) in relation to\nan industrial chemical that is, or contains, a GM product.\n\n(2) Subject to subsection (5), the Director must give written notice to\nthe Gene Technology Regulator:\n\n(a) stating that the assessment is to be undertaken, or that the\napplication for the permit has been made, as the case\nrequires; and\n\n(b) requesting the Gene Technology Regulator to give advice\nabout the assessment or the application for the permit.\n\n(3) If the Director gives the Gene Technology Regulator a notice under\nsubsection (2), the Gene Technology Regulator may give written\nadvice to the Director about the assessment or the application.\n\n(4) The advice is to be given within the period specified in the notice.\n\n(5) If an advice from the Gene Technology Regulator is in force under\nsection 10B in relation to a class of GM products, the Director is\nnot required to notify the Regulator under this section in relation\nto:\n\n(a) an assessment of an industrial chemical that is or contains a\nGM product belonging to that class; or\n\n(b) an application for a permit in respect of an industrial\nchemical that is or contains a GM product belonging to that\nclass.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-consequential-amendments-act-2000-sch-1-sec-10a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-consequential-amendments-act-2000-sch-1-sec-10a-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-consequential-amendments-act-2000-sch-1-sec-10a-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-consequential-amendments-act-2000-sch-1-sec-10a-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-consequential-amendments-act-2000-sch-1-sec-10a-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "97645f2799d45237bacd7743a0783265f32078fb6b9c62aa5d0ad75ab0c5b513"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-consequential-amendments-act-2000#sch-1-sec-10a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "10A Consultation with Gene Technology Regulator",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 11,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies to the following:\n\n(a) an assessment of an industrial chemical that is, or contains, a\nGM product;\n\n(b) an application for a permit (however described) in relation to\nan industrial chemical that is, or contains, a GM product.\n\n(2) Subject to subsection (5), the Director must give written notice to\nthe Gene Technology Regulator:\n\n(a) stating that the assessment is to be undertaken, or that the\napplication for the permit has been made, as the case\nrequires; and\n\n(b) requesting the Gene Technology Regulator to give advice\nabout the assessment or the application for the permit.\n\n(3) If the Director gives the Gene Technology Regulator a notice under\nsubsection (2), the Gene Technology Regulator may give written\nadvice to the Director about the assessment or the application.\n\n(4) The advice is to be given within the period specified in the notice.\n\n(5) If an advice from the Gene Technology Regulator is in force under\nsection 10B in relation to a class of GM products, the Director is\nnot required to notify the Regulator under this section in relation\nto:\n\n(a) an assessment of an industrial chemical that is or contains a\nGM product belonging to that class; or\n\n(b) an application for a permit in respect of an industrial\nchemical that is or contains a GM product belonging to that\nclass."
    },
