    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-consequential-amendments-act-2000-sch-1-sec-10a-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "10A(5) Consultation with Gene Technology Regulator",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-consequential-amendments-act-2000#sch-1-sec-10a-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "gene-technology-consequential-amendments-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "gene-technology-consequential-amendments-act-2000.pdf, p.11",
      "values:originalText": "(5) If an advice from the Gene Technology Regulator is in force under\nsection 10B in relation to a class of GM products, the Director is\nnot required to notify the Regulator under this section in relation\nto:\n\n(a) an assessment of an industrial chemical that is or contains a\nGM product belonging to that class; or\n\n(b) an application for a permit in respect of an industrial\nchemical that is or contains a GM product belonging to that\nclass.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) If an advice from the Gene Technology Regulator is in force under\nsection 10B in relation to a class of GM products, the Director is\nnot required to notify the Regulator under this section in relation\nto:\n\n(a) an assessment of an industrial chemical that is or contains a\nGM product belonging to that class; or\n\n(b) an application for a permit in respect of an industrial\nchemical that is or contains a GM product belonging to that\nclass.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:gene-technology-consequential-amendments-act-2000-sch-1-sec-10a"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-consequential-amendments-act-2000-sch-1-sec-10a-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-consequential-amendments-act-2000-sch-1-sec-10a-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-consequential-amendments-act-2000-sch-1-sec-10a-ss-5-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "cb6d027a6eca6103e67810c203cda14e864a3785c56da7ad88967176a03d0a37",
      "skos:note": "Exemption from notification for certain GM product assessments and applications."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-consequential-amendments-act-2000#sch-1-sec-10a-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "10A(5) Consultation with Gene Technology Regulator",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 11,
      "values:originalText": "(5) If an advice from the Gene Technology Regulator is in force under\nsection 10B in relation to a class of GM products, the Director is\nnot required to notify the Regulator under this section in relation\nto:\n\n(a) an assessment of an industrial chemical that is or contains a\nGM product belonging to that class; or\n\n(b) an application for a permit in respect of an industrial\nchemical that is or contains a GM product belonging to that\nclass."
    },
