    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-consequential-amendments-act-2000-sch-1-sec-10b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "10B Director may seek advice about classes of GM products",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-consequential-amendments-act-2000#sch-1-sec-10b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "gene-technology-consequential-amendments-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "gene-technology-consequential-amendments-act-2000.pdf, p.11",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Director may request advice from the Gene Technology\nRegulator in relation to industrial chemicals that consist of, or that\n\nSchedule 1  Consequential amendments\n\ncontain, a GM product belonging to a class of GM products\nspecified in the request.\n\n(2) A request for advice under subsection (1) must specify the matters\nto which the advice is to relate.\n\n(3) If the Director requests advice from the Gene Technology\nRegulator under subsection (1), the Gene Technology Regulator\nmay provide written advice in relation to the matters specified in\nthe request.\n\n(4) If the Gene Technology Regulator gives advice to the Director\nunder subsection (3), the advice remains in force until it is\nwithdrawn by the Gene Technology Regulator by written notice\ngiven to the Director.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Director may request advice from the Gene Technology\nRegulator in relation to industrial chemicals that consist of, or that\n\nSchedule 1  Consequential amendments\n\ncontain, a GM product belonging to a class of GM products\nspecified in the request.\n\n(2) A request for advice under subsection (1) must specify the matters\nto which the advice is to relate.\n\n(3) If the Director requests advice from the Gene Technology\nRegulator under subsection (1), the Gene Technology Regulator\nmay provide written advice in relation to the matters specified in\nthe request.\n\n(4) If the Gene Technology Regulator gives advice to the Director\nunder subsection (3), the advice remains in force until it is\nwithdrawn by the Gene Technology Regulator by written notice\ngiven to the Director.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-consequential-amendments-act-2000-sch-1-sec-10b-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-consequential-amendments-act-2000-sch-1-sec-10b-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-consequential-amendments-act-2000-sch-1-sec-10b-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-consequential-amendments-act-2000-sch-1-sec-10b-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c2d3263a577b1655e6874911b36d763d6c071091cdd4d57628afe10c0ea492de"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-consequential-amendments-act-2000#sch-1-sec-10b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "10B Director may seek advice about classes of GM products",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 11,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Director may request advice from the Gene Technology\nRegulator in relation to industrial chemicals that consist of, or that\n\nSchedule 1  Consequential amendments\n\ncontain, a GM product belonging to a class of GM products\nspecified in the request.\n\n(2) A request for advice under subsection (1) must specify the matters\nto which the advice is to relate.\n\n(3) If the Director requests advice from the Gene Technology\nRegulator under subsection (1), the Gene Technology Regulator\nmay provide written advice in relation to the matters specified in\nthe request.\n\n(4) If the Gene Technology Regulator gives advice to the Director\nunder subsection (3), the advice remains in force until it is\nwithdrawn by the Gene Technology Regulator by written notice\ngiven to the Director."
    },
