    {
      "@id": "concept:gene-technology-consequential-amendments-act-2000-sch-1-sec-30d",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "30D Secretary may seek advice about classes of GM products",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-consequential-amendments-act-2000#sch-1-sec-30d"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "gene-technology-consequential-amendments-act-2000.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "gene-technology-consequential-amendments-act-2000.pdf, p.13",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Secretary may request advice from the Gene Technology\nRegulator in relation to therapeutic goods that consist of, or that\ncontain, a GM product belonging to a class of GM products\nspecified in the request.\n\n(2) A request for advice under subsection (1) must specify the matters\nto which the advice is to relate.\n\n(3) If the Secretary requests advice from the Gene Technology\nRegulator under subsection (1), the Gene Technology Regulator\n\nSchedule 1  Consequential amendments\n\nmay provide written advice in relation to the matters specified in\nthe request.\n\n(4) If the Gene Technology Regulator gives advice to the Secretary\nunder subsection (3), the advice remains in force until it is\nwithdrawn by the Gene Technology Regulator by written notice\ngiven to the Secretary.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Secretary may request advice from the Gene Technology\nRegulator in relation to therapeutic goods that consist of, or that\ncontain, a GM product belonging to a class of GM products\nspecified in the request.\n\n(2) A request for advice under subsection (1) must specify the matters\nto which the advice is to relate.\n\n(3) If the Secretary requests advice from the Gene Technology\nRegulator under subsection (1), the Gene Technology Regulator\n\nSchedule 1  Consequential amendments\n\nmay provide written advice in relation to the matters specified in\nthe request.\n\n(4) If the Gene Technology Regulator gives advice to the Secretary\nunder subsection (3), the advice remains in force until it is\nwithdrawn by the Gene Technology Regulator by written notice\ngiven to the Secretary.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-consequential-amendments-act-2000-sch-1-sec-30d-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-consequential-amendments-act-2000-sch-1-sec-30d-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-consequential-amendments-act-2000-sch-1-sec-30d-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:gene-technology-consequential-amendments-act-2000-sch-1-sec-30d-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2d50751445b8daa4c4f157126beb49c070e1eab21856aee9cf238420100884c4"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/gene-technology-consequential-amendments-act-2000#sch-1-sec-30d",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "30D Secretary may seek advice about classes of GM products",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 13,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Secretary may request advice from the Gene Technology\nRegulator in relation to therapeutic goods that consist of, or that\ncontain, a GM product belonging to a class of GM products\nspecified in the request.\n\n(2) A request for advice under subsection (1) must specify the matters\nto which the advice is to relate.\n\n(3) If the Secretary requests advice from the Gene Technology\nRegulator under subsection (1), the Gene Technology Regulator\n\nSchedule 1  Consequential amendments\n\nmay provide written advice in relation to the matters specified in\nthe request.\n\n(4) If the Gene Technology Regulator gives advice to the Secretary\nunder subsection (3), the advice remains in force until it is\nwithdrawn by the Gene Technology Regulator by written notice\ngiven to the Secretary."
    },
